course: dictionary
lesson: 8339
title: Romany and Romani people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «Romany» has three uses. A Romany is one person from the Romani people, also called Roma. Romany is also the name of their language. And Romany can describe things that belong to them, such as a Romany caravan.
explain: The Romani people came from India long ago and spread through Europe and the world. Some still travel, but many live settled lives in one place, so do not assume that every Romani person is a traveller.
explain: Use the respectful names «Romani» or «Roma». The older word «gypsy» can hurt people, even when you find it in an old book. Judge people as individuals, not by an old idea about a whole people.
fact: A Romany is a member of the Romani people, who are also called Roma.
fact: «Romany» is also the name of the Romani language, which is related to languages of India.
fact: When «Romany» describes something, it means of the Romani people, as in «a Romany caravan».
fact: The Romani people came to Britain about 500 years ago, as one of the example sentences says.
fact: Many Romani people were murdered in the Holocaust, so their history deserves respect and careful telling.
exercise: The Romani people came from long ago in which country? | *India | Italy | Spain | Norway
exercise: Which name is the respectful one for Romani people? | Gypsy | *Romani | Caravaner | Wanderer
exercise: What does Romany describe in «a Romany caravan»? | A kind of horse | A time of year | Painted in bright colours | *Of the Romani people
test: Are all Romani people travellers? | They travel only in summer | *No, many live settled lives | Only the old ones travel | Yes, every one of them travels
test: Why is judging a whole people by an old idea unfair? | It makes books longer | All ideas about people are true | *Each person is different, and an old idea may not be true | It is always easy to do
exam: Which sentence talks about Romani people most respectfully? | The Romany wagons are only for us | The gypsies are all thieves | Those travellers are strange and should be avoided | *Romani people have their own language, music and traditions
